message: "If you use this software or the saved runs in your research, please cite it."
title: "TR-Benchmarking: clustering how language models reason about legal questions"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-05
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/at350/tr-benchmarking"
authors:
  - family-names: Tai
    given-names: Alan
  - name: "DavidL0417"
  - family-names: Hanlon
    given-names: Clark
keywords:
  - legal reasoning
  - large language models
  - evaluation
  - clustering
  - instruction-tuned embeddings
  - IRAC
abstract: >-
  A research toolkit that samples many answers to one legal question from several
  language models, embeds them with an instruction-tuned encoder, clusters the
  embeddings with UMAP and HDBSCAN, and reports the distinct lines of reasoning the
  models took, including an adversarial test with deliberately wrong answers and a
  source-grounded rubric workflow with a browsable portal.
